  "output": "The book follows a magitech artificer who takes a routine guild job in a ruin that is \"folded out of space and stuck in a single looping hour\" [1]. The story is set in the guild-city of Threnn, where magic is a \"shattered art\" divided into tiers called Facets, some of which are forbidden or lost [4]. The plot involves a party taking a commission at \"the Nine,\" discovering something is wrong, and dealing with a loop, a survivor, and a \"Keystone\" [3].\n\nThe protagonist is Cael Ferren [2], a 26-year-old brass-rank artificer [5]. Cael possesses the secret ability to feel \"deep Facets\" of magic—a sensation she describes as a \"hum\" or a \"struck fork\" [1, 5]. Having spent her life hiding this ability because she believed it was a \"sickness\" that the Wardens were right to remove, her journey involves learning that this ability is actually a \"compass to a magic the world broke on purpose\" [5].",
